  "result": "I implemented `slugify` in `src/strings.js` and added 10 tests for it in `test/strings.test.js`. `npm test` passes, with 12 of 12 tests green (the 10 new ones plus the 2 existing `capitalize` tests).\n\nIt lowercases, strips diacritics (`đ` and `Đ` become `d`), and turns each run of non-`a-z0-9` characters into one hyphen. It then trims the leading hyphen, cuts to 50 characters, and trims any trailing hyphen left by the cut.\n\nThe tests cover:\n- Vietnamese and other Latin diacritics\n- symbol runs and trimming\n- digits\n- input made only of symbols, which returns an empty string\n- the 50-character cut, including a case where the cut lands on a hyphen",
